## 4b. Platform prerequisites (build first, in this order)

- P0.1 Toolchain pins: Rust + LiteSVM + Anchor versions pinned, Cargo.lock committed, L1 `.so` prebuilt with digest BEFORE any UI work.
- P0.2 SQLite schema: `users(nickname UNIQUE, wallet NULL, created)` · `sessions(uuid, user, room, created, expires, reaped)` · `attempts(session, code_hash, verdict, at)` · `hints_used(session, hint_n)` · `solves(user, room, points, first_at)` · `findings(user, room, severity, proof, fix, solver_hash, at)`.
- P0.3 Session handling: UUID per Run, fresh keypairs/program IDs per session, 900s TTL + reaper sweeper, per-IP caps, localhost-bound, flag/solver never leaves server.
- P0.4 API skeleton: `POST /run` (exploit → verdict) · `POST /finding` → issues proof · `GET /proof/:hash` (public) · `GET /board` · `GET /rooms` · static frontend. One small server, no framework ceremony.
- P0.5 Content pack: L1 + L2 (owner-check) vuln+fixed pairs + exploit templates TODOs + 101 lesson markdown + 3 staged hints per room + room card metadata (tier/points/prereq), all with attribution headers.
- P0.6 Evidence logger: append-only rows from 11:00 Sat (hypothesis → test → result, exact commands + outputs, failures verbatim) — feeds Sunday's README.
- P0.7 Sunday prep built Saturday: offline fallback bundle (frozen transcript + local LiteSVM run, no net) + recorded offline demo + production site live for judges/users + `VENDOR_NOTICES` + AI disclosure draft.
- P0.8 Deck + pitch: 3 core slides (Problem+result / Demo flow / Impact-next test) + 4+3+1 rehearsal Sunday 11:00–13:00.
- P0.9 Production site live (Sunday-critical path, not a footnote): static frontend + one API process + SQLite file on a reachable host; public URL printed in deck + QR (target: Sun 10:00, before 11:00 freeze); `/health` endpoint green; venue demo runs against RECORDED video first, live site second; fallback = same bundle served from team laptop over hotspot if venue net/host dies. Deploy Saturday evening if humanly possible — Sunday morning is for evidence, not DevOps.
- P0.10 Database (locked): the SQLite file from P0.2 IS the production database — it lives next to the API process, no DB server, no Postgres, no migrations ceremony (back up by copying the file). Stateless/ephemeral host → Turso free tier (SQLite-compatible, one connection string). Laptop fallback serves the same file. Decision rationale: a managed DB buys zero rubric points and costs Sunday-morning DevOps hours.

## 5. Explicitly NOT (kill list)

No mention of Sui or any other chain on any public surface, deck, or proof page (Solana grant positioning — locked 2026-10-03). No live L2/L3 (stub cards), no leaderboard-as-hiring (ranks = progress only, P2 forbids auto-ranking), no certificate PDF (proof URL instead), no wallet login (skip auth entirely — H02 has no such requirement), no team dashboard (one screenshot mock for story max), no video platform, no custom grader language.
Cut 2026-10-03 (farming/simplicity): NO public writeup library — browsing others' solves is forbidden (points > 0 beats learning); your OWN submitted finding stays (it is the P2 proof artifact, not a library). No first-run tour, no account/settings page, no upload UI (challenges ship as static files), no teams/clans.

### 5b. Out of MVP scope entirely (deck-roadmap slides only, zero Saturday code)

- **Blitz arena (timed 24/48h, seasonal board).** Design locked in `web3-security-platform/13-arena-and-rating-design.md` (two ladders: Mastery permanent + Arena CTFtime-style; speed bonuses live only inside windows; rooms join permanent pool at base value after). No standing-pool timed security arena exists on any chain (verified) — this is the post-H02 moat. H02 builds room one that blitzes will reuse; blitz itself is slide + §9 next-test, never sprint work.

## 6. Build order (Lazar = harness/verifier/demo; Ognjen = page/pitch/deck)

1. Now → 17:00: P0.1–P0.5 (harness + prebuilt `.so` + verifier with negative control green) + page skeleton with Run wired (F2.2 shell).
2. 17:00 → 19:00: F1 real content + F3 form/proof + first end-to-end (stranger test #1). 19:00 SCOPE FREEZE — F1–F3 as-is.
3. Evening: honest test (5 beginners, 3/5-in-10min), P0.6 rows, P0.7 offline bundle.
4. Sun 09:30 → 11:00: evidence README chain, disclosure, P0.8 deck; 11:00 CODE & EVIDENCE FREEZE; pitch rehearsal.

## 7. The one honest test

5 beginners at venue, each gets URL + 10 min, no help beyond built-in hints. Record: pointed at bug? (y/n + time), pointed at fix? (y/n), proof URL produced? Pass bar 3/5. Log every failure verbatim.

## 8. Risks (3 max)

1. Anchor/LiteSVM version churn eats hours → pin versions + Cargo.lock first, prebuild `.so` before any UI work.
2. Venue WiFi dies → offline fallback is a submission item, build it Saturday, not Sunday.
3. Verifier false-green → negative control is load-bearing; no green claim without fixed-code-must-fail demonstrated.

