## 10. Next test (the one experiment after H02)

Do 20 strangers finish L1 unassisted and do 5 produce L3-ready findings — decides whether L2/L3 get built or the format is wrong.
Second: timed blitz arena. Timed non-EVM CTFs exist only as one-offs (MoveCTF 2022: 345 players/4 chals; MoveCTF 2024: 527 teams/8 chals/48h/$4.5k — nothing since; Paradigm Solhana 1-3 + Pool inside a multi-chain event; picoCTF Solfire and justCTF Darksols/Lamports as single challenges; one-day Solana CTF Bengaluru Jul 2025). No recurring always-on timed arena for non-EVM exists — weekend blitzes with sponsored pools are the post-H02 game mode, H02 builds only the always-on Easy room that blitzes reuse.

## 11. Team locks part 2 — 2026-10-03 (operator calls)

- Rooms: 2 LIVE (port from MIT repos; more iff time). Room 2 default = owner-check Medium (`z0neSec programs/owner-check/`), second verifier predicate required.
- Execution principle: hermetic always — LiteSVM in-process, zero real money, zero real transactions, zero devnet. Behavior-identical emulation is explicitly allowed wherever it preserves verdict semantics.
- Certs: web2-app only, never on-chain (proof URL + profile badges).
- Backend: simplest monolith that works (stack: SvelteKit — locked 2026-10-03; rCTF never a fork).
- DB/hosting: $0 total. PRIMARY = HuggingFace Spaces free (one Docker image: API + static; 2vCPU/16GB; sleep after 48h idle covers the whole event) + Turso free tier (SQLite over HTTP — data survives sleep/restarts; ephemeral container disk must never hold the only copy). REJECTED: Vercel for API (serverless can't run LiteSVM process/SQLite file — static only, and two deploy targets lose Saturday), Fly.io (no free tier for new signups + card), Render free (15-min sleep + ephemeral disk wipes SQLite + free PG expires in 30d), Oracle free VM (best raw free, but account setup + ARM + ops burns Saturday). FALLBACK = Cloudflare Tunnel to team laptop (free, zero deploy). No custom domain (subdomain printed in deck + QR).
- CI per ARCHITECTURE_PROFILE (fast gate, no waits): PR-triggered + agent-requested runs only. Gate = fmt + clippy/vitest + unit + L1 cargo tests incl. negative control, target <3 min. Full battery (mutation ≥40% on verifier crate, fuzz, audit/deny) exists as workflow but runs nightly/manual — never in the dev loop. No long waits between tests and development, ever.
- TS↔Rust bridge (review `17` BLOCKER 1 — PROPOSED for S5 lock): PRIMARY = official `node-litesvm` npm wrapper (maintained by LiteSVM team, no hand-rolled binding); FALLBACK = per-Run child-process JSON bridge (Rust binary beside server, exec budget inside the 30–60s kill window; still one container — "no second process" governs deployment topology, not per-request children); napi-rs hand-rolled binding REJECTED for 24h (toolchain-debug risk). Canary before verifier code: hello-world through the picked mechanism in the target Node 22 + Docker base, GO/NO-GO decides.

